From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MAGIC Grants <info@magicgrants.org>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 14:27:43 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] Remove libunbound DNS resolution

monero_c no longer links libunbound. Skylight and Spice resolve OpenAlias
in the app (DNSSEC over Tor), so the library's own resolver was dead
weight: a recursive DNSSEC resolver with a steady stream of security
advisories, which would also send DNS queries outside Tor if anything
ever called it.

DNSResolver keeps its API so every caller compiles unchanged, but each
lookup now returns no records and reports DNSSEC as unavailable. OpenAlias
resolution (WalletManager::resolveOpenAlias), checkUpdates and DNS
checkpoints find nothing. tools::on_startup() no longer creates a
libunbound context to check whether it was built with threads, and CMake
no longer requires, includes or links libunbound.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
